# Build context of this Dockerfile: the REPO ROOT (#3425) — the builder runs
# scripts/ops/go_build.sh, the one place the repo's `go build` flags are
# written, and that file sits outside this module directory. Docker BuildKit
# reads THIS file (`<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`, next to the Dockerfile) in
# place of the context root's .dockerignore, so the context stays what it was
# before the move — this module — plus that one script.
#
# Allowlist: exclude everything, re-include what the Dockerfile COPYs.
# Requires BuildKit (CI uses docker/setup-buildx; Docker 23+ defaults to it);
# the legacy builder ignores this file and would send the root context.
*
!scripts/ops/go_build.sh
!components/threshold-exporter/app/

# Container SAST baseline (epic #448 / TRK-311): the `*` above already covers
# .git/ .github/ scripts/ tests/ docs/ at the root; these keep stray docs,
# logs and env files out of the re-included module, at any depth.
**/*.md
**/*.log
**/.env*
